---
import DocumentIcon from './DocumentIcon.astro';
---

<!-- Feature Comparison Table -->
    <section class="comparison-section">
      <h2>Feature Comparison</h2>
      <table class="comparison-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Feature</th>
            <th>Free</th>
            <th>Pro</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="feature-name">Local notes</td>
            <td>Unlimited</td>
            <td>Unlimited</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="feature-name">Locked notes</td>
            <td>Up to 5</td>
            <td>Unlimited</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="feature-name">Real-time cloud sync</td>
            <td><span class="x-icon">✕</span></td>
            <td><span class="check-icon">✓</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <!-- Why We Charge Section -->
    <section class="why-pay-section">
      <h2>Why Do We Charge?</h2>
      <p>
        Better Keep Notes is built with care by a small team. We believe in honest, sustainable software—no ads, no data
        selling,
        no dark patterns. Here's where your subscription goes:
      </p>
      <div class="why-cards">
        <div class="why-card">
          <DocumentIcon name="server" />
          <h3>Server Infrastructure</h3>
          <p>Cloud sync and real-time features require servers that cost real money to run and maintain securely.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <DocumentIcon name="shield-check" />
          <h3>End-to-End Encryption</h3>
          <p>Strong encryption is computationally expensive. We invest in proper cryptography to keep your data truly
            private.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <DocumentIcon name="code-2" />
          <h3>Ongoing Development</h3>
          <p>New features, bug fixes, and cross-platform support across 6 platforms takes continuous effort.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <DocumentIcon name="ban" />
          <h3>No Ads, No Tracking</h3>
          <p>Your subscription means we never need to monetize your attention or data. You're the customer, not the
            product.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Free Forever Section -->
    <section class="free-forever">
      <h2> Free Forever</h2>
      <p>
        These features will always be free, no account required:
      </p>
      <div class="free-features">
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Unlimited local notes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Local encryption</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>5 locked notes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Labels & colors</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Pin notes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Reminders</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Read-only mode</span>
        </div>
        <div class="free-feature">
          <DocumentIcon name="check" />
          <span>Works offline</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Can I use the app without creating an account?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! Better Keep Notes works completely offline without any account. All free features are available without
          signing up. You only need an account if you want to sync your notes across devices.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>What happens when my Pro subscription expires?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Your notes are always yours. When your subscription expires, you'll still have access to all your local notes.
          Cloud sync will pause, but your data remains safe and encrypted locally. You can export everything at any
          time.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Is there a free trial for Pro?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! New users get a 7-day free trial of Pro features. No credit card required to start. If you decide Pro
          isn't for you, you'll automatically switch to the free plan.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Can I switch between monthly and yearly billing?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes, you can change your billing cycle at any time. If you switch from monthly to yearly, you'll get a
          prorated credit for your remaining monthly subscription.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Can I self-host Better Keep Notes?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! If you're interested in running your own backend with Firebase or Supabase, please contact us at
          <a href="mailto:contact@betterkeep.app">contact@betterkeep.app</a> and we'll
          help you get set up.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span>Can I get a refund?</span>
          <DocumentIcon name="chevron-down" />
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes. If you're not satisfied within the first 30 days, contact us for a full refund. For subscriptions
          purchased through app stores, refunds are processed according to their respective policies.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
